      {
        "finding_id": "section-6ba5daec718cb8e2a9ea",
        "file": "ournavybarbaryco00alle_ournavybarbaryco00alle_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Our navy and the Barbary corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/ournavybarbaryco00alle",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Allen, Gardner Weld, 1856-1944"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1905-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "e15e3a557e79edec2ea71b2b5ccd1015a5ec882a666c35aba27115b05eadb074",
        "evidence_excerpt": "At  last,  informed  of  the  added  dangers  to  com- \nmerce, the  House  of  Representatives,  January  2, \n1794,  resolved  by  a  majority  of  two  \"  that  a  naval \nforce,  adequate  to  the  protection  of  the  commerce  of \nthe  United  States  against  the  Algerine  corsairs,  ought \nto  be  provided.\"  A  bill  was  reported  January  20  by \nthe  Committee  of  Ways  and  Means  providing  for  the \nconstruction  of  six  vessels  at  a  cost  of  six  hundred \nthousand  dollars.  The  opponents  argued  that  the \nfinances  of  the  country  did  not  justify  the  expense, \nand  that   the  public  debt  must  first  be  discharged ;",
        "years_in_scope": [],
