      {
        "finding_id": "section-1122f68948337bb982fc",
        "file": "ournavybarbaryco00alle_ournavybarbaryco00alle_djvu.txt",
        "title": "Our navy and the Barbary corsairs",
        "url": "https://archive.org/details/ournavybarbaryco00alle",
        "source_bibliography": {
          "creator": [
            "Allen, Gardner Weld, 1856-1944"
          ],
          "date": [
            "1905-01-01T00:00:00Z"
          ],
          "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
          "evidence_level": null,
          "rights": null
        },
        "source_text_sha256": "e15e3a557e79edec2ea71b2b5ccd1015a5ec882a666c35aba27115b05eadb074",
        "evidence_excerpt": "Humphreys,  not  wishing  to  assume  the  responsibility \nof  the  frigate  to  be  presented  to  the  dey,  sent  O'Brien \nto  America  in  the  Sophia  to  refer  the  matter  to  the \ngovernment.  Upon  receiving  the  report,  Timothy \nPickering,  secretary  of  state,  wrote  to  Humphreys \nJune  11, 1796  :  \"  There  appears  no  eligible  alternative \nbut  to  confirm  the  engagement  of  Messrs.  Barlow  and \nDonaldson.\"  O'Brien  returned  to  Lisbon  in  July.  In \nthe  mean  time  Humphreys  had  succeeded  in  negotiating \nbills  on  London  in  Lisbon  for  two  hundred  and  twenty- \nfive  thousand  dollars.  This  was  embarked  on  the \nSophia,  and  O'Brien  set  sail  for  Algiers  August  4. \nOn  the  way  he  was  captured  by  a  Tripolitan  corsair \nand  taken  into  Tripoli.  Another  American  vessel \nwas  taken  about  the  same  time.  The  pasha  of  Tripoli \nwas  loath  to  give  up  such  a  rich  prize,  but  he  dared  not \ndisregard  O'Brien's  Algerine  passport ;  so  after  hold- \ning him  three  weeks,  he  released  him,  and  the  Sophia \narrived  safely  at  Algiers  in  October.  The  treaty  stipu- \nlations were  now  fulfilled,  and  the  dey  was  so  pleased \nthat  he  offered  to  lend  Barlow  ninety  thousand  piastres",
        "years_in_scope": [],
        "date_basis": "EXPLICIT_PARAGRAPH",
        "date_evidence": null,
        "matched_names": [],
        "name_basis": "THEMATIC_CONCEPT",
