            "evidence_kind": "ACQUIRED_TEXT_EXCERPT",
            "source_key": "da777bf33a44b340e528",
            "source_type": "OCR_CONTEXT",
            "text": "At  the  beginning  of  the  17th  century,  La  Mamora,  located  at  the  mouth  of  the \nSebou  River  a  few  leagues  north  of  Sale,  was  among  the  most  formidable  pirate  haunts \non  the  Atlantic  coast  of  Morocco.  It  had  welcomed  the  pirates  of  Larache  after  that  port \nwas  granted  to  the  Spaniards  in  1610.  This  “ Pirate  Republic to  use  the  expression  of \nThomas  Le  Gendre,  was  unique  in  that  it  belonged  to  everyone;  those  who  wanted  refuge",
            "locator_status": "ACQUIRED_TEXT_RANGE",
